                prev_x, cur_x = prev, cur
            elif cur.val == y and cur_y is None:
                prev_y, cur_y = prev, cur
            prev, cur = cur, cur.next
        if cur_x is None or cur_y is None:
            return
        if prev_x: prev_x.next = cur_y
        else:      self.head = cur_y
        if prev_y: prev_y.next = cur_x
        else:      self.head = cur_x
        cur_x.next, cur_y.next = cur_y.next, cur_x.next

The swap relinks nodes rather than copying payloads — that is the whole point of the question. One pass finds each target and its predecessor; then each predecessor (or the head, if a target is first) is repointed at the other node and the two next pointers are exchanged. Written in that order, the adjacent-node case — where one node's predecessor IS the other node — falls out correctly with no special-casing. O(n) time, O(1) extra space.

