O(n) time, O(1) space DP. dp[i] = min cost to stand on step i = cost[i] + min(dp[i-1], dp[i-2]), with dp[0] = cost[0], dp[1] = cost[1]; the answer is min(dp[n-1], dp[n-2]) because the top of the floor is index n, reachable from either of the last two steps.

def minCostClimbingStairs(cost):
    a = b = 0                 # cheapest way to reach steps i-2 and i-1
    for c in cost:
        a, b = b, min(a, b) + c
    return min(a, b)

